# Board viewport layout and scale

Refine both fixed zoom levels and allow Detail panning beneath persistent Board controls.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Detail uses a visibly higher fixed zoom level than the current implementation.
- [ ] Detail panning can move board content behind Done, edit controls, help, and player selection.
- [ ] Persistent controls remain fixed, visually above the board, fully legible, and interactive.
- [ ] Pan bounds still prevent losing the board entirely and permit reaching every playable edge and vertex.
- [ ] Overview shifts slightly upward and appears visually centred in the complete screen layout.
- [ ] View and edit modes share consistent board geometry without jumping when mode changes.
- [ ] Tap-to-focus, long-hold radial editing, and immediate Detail pan arbitration remain unchanged.
- [ ] Deterministic viewport tests compile and focused gesture/layout checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Keep the two-level discrete pinch model; continuous zoom is not requested.
